{"title": "Quant Super Practice — Mock #124", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Rupesh purchased raw materials for a certain price to manufacture a product. However, due to labor shortage, 27.5% of the raw materials could not be utilized and was wasted. 60% of the cost of raw materials used was added as the manufacturing cost. If Rupesh could sell his product at a price to earn an overall profit of 40% after offering a discount of 20%, how many times (round off 3 decimal places) the total cost of the raw materials purchased was the marked price of the product?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2370;&#2346;&#2375;&#2358; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2404; &#2361;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2325;&#2367;, &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339;, 27.5% &#2325;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2361;&#2379; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2325;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; 60% &#2357;&#2367;&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;&#2339; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346;&#2375;&#2358; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; 40% &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2325;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; (3 &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;) &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2341;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["2.511", "2.421", "2.342", "2.652"], "options_hi": ["2.511", "2.421", "2.342", "2.652"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let Rupesh purchase 100 kg of raw material at Rs. 1 per kg.</p><p>Total C.P = 100 * 1 = Rs. 100</p><p>C.P of used raw material = 100 * 72.5/100 = Rs. 72.5 </p><p>Manufacturing cost = 100 + (72.5 * 60/100) = Rs. 143.5 </p><p>S.P = 143.5 * 140/100 = Rs. 200.9</p><p>M.P = 200.9 * 100/80 = Rs. 251.125 </p><p>Hence, the required value = 251.125/100 = 2.511</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let Rupesh purchase 100 kg of raw material at Rs. 1 per kg.</p><p>Total C.P = 100 * 1 = Rs. 100</p><p>C.P of used raw material = 100 * 72.5/100 = Rs. 72.5 </p><p>Manufacturing cost = 100 + (72.5 * 60/100) = Rs. 143.5 </p><p>S.P = 143.5 * 140/100 = Rs. 200.9</p><p>M.P = 200.9 * 100/80 = Rs. 251.125 </p><p>Hence, the required value = 251.125/100 = 2.511</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper offers 3 schemes of discounts to his customers. Which of the following schemes will fetch the minimum discount percentage?</p><p>I. Two successive discounts of 25% and 32%</p><p>II. Buy 6 get 5 free.</p><p>III. Buy 8 get 7 free.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; 3 &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2327;&#2368;?</p><p>I. 25% &#2324;&#2352; 32% &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335;</p><p>II. 6 &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375;&#2306; 5 &#2350;&#2369;&#2347;&#2364;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p>III. 8 &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375;&#2306; 7 &#2350;&#2369;&#2347;&#2364;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["I", "II", "III", "Both II and III"], "options_hi": ["I", "II", "III", "II &#2324;&#2352; III &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>I. Effective discount = 25 + 32  -  (25 * 32)/100 = 49%</p><p>II. Total items = 11, Paid = 6</p><p>Discount = 5 * 100/11 = 45.45%</p><p>III. Total items = 15, paid = 8 </p><p>Discount = 7 * 100/15 = 46.67% </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>I. Effective discount = 25 + 32  -  (25 * 32)/100 = 49%</p><p>II. Total items = 11, Paid = 6</p><p>Discount = 5 * 100/11 = 45.45%</p><p>III. Total items = 15, paid = 8 </p><p>Discount = 7 * 100/15 = 46.67% </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the single discount rate percentage equivalent to the successive discounts of 10%, 25%, and 18%.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>10%, 25% &#2324;&#2352; 18% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325;&#2354; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["62.25%", "55.50%", "44.65%", "37.50%"], "options_hi": ["62.25%", "55.50%", "44.65%", "37.50%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Equivalent Discount = 1  -  (1  -  10/100) * (1  -  25/100) * (1  -  18/100) </p><p>= 1  -  0.9 * 0.75 * 0.82 </p><p>= 0.4465 </p><p>Hence, the required percentage = 44.65% </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Equivalent Discount = 1  -  (1  -  10/100) * (1  -  25/100) * (1  -  18/100) </p><p>= 1  -  0.9 * 0.75 * 0.82 </p><p>= 0.4465 </p><p>Hence, the required percentage = 44.65% </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The marked price of an article is 32% more than its cost price. If a discount of 18% is given, what will be the profit percentage?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 32% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 18% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["7(6/25) %", "9(6/25) %", "5(6/25) %", "8(6/25) %"], "options_hi": ["7(6/25) %", "9(6/25) %", "5(6/25) %", "8(6/25) %"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let C.P. be Rs. 100</p><p>M.P = C.P * 132/100 = 100 * 132/100 = Rs. 132 </p><p>S.P = M.P * (100  -  18)/100 = 132 * (100  -  18)/100 = Rs. 108.24 </p><p>Hence, the required profit = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C. P </p><p>= (108.24  -  100) * 100/100 </p><p>= 206/25%</p><p>= 8(6/25) % </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let C.P. be Rs. 100</p><p>M.P = C.P * 132/100 = 100 * 132/100 = Rs. 132 </p><p>S.P = M.P * (100  -  18)/100 = 132 * (100  -  18)/100 = Rs. 108.24 </p><p>Hence, the required profit = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C. P </p><p>= (108.24  -  100) * 100/100 </p><p>= 206/25%</p><p>= 8(6/25) % </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A toy is marked for Rs. 3200. A customer pays Rs. 1904. If the customer got a series of two discounts and the rate of the first discount is 15%, then the rate of the second discount is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2367;&#2354;&#2380;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 3200 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; 1904 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; 15% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["30%", "25%", "20%", "40%"], "options_hi": ["30%", "25%", "20%", "40%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>S.P = C.P * (100  -  Discount)/100 </p><p>1904 = 3200 * (100  -  Discount)/100 </p><p>100  -  Discount = 59.5 </p><p>Discount = 40.5 </p><p>Effective discount = X + Y  -  (X * Y)/100 </p><p>40.5 = 15 + Y  -  (15 * Y)/100 </p><p>0.85Y = 25.5 </p><p>Y = 30% </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>S.P = C.P * (100  -  Discount)/100 </p><p>1904 = 3200 * (100  -  Discount)/100 </p><p>100  -  Discount = 59.5 </p><p>Discount = 40.5 </p><p>Effective discount = X + Y  -  (X * Y)/100 </p><p>40.5 = 15 + Y  -  (15 * Y)/100 </p><p>0.85Y = 25.5 </p><p>Y = 30% </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>On the tag price, a seller offers a 15% discount and a cashback of &#8377;450. He still earns 10% profit. If the cost price is Rs. 1800, then the tag price (rounded off to 2 decimal places) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2335;&#2376;&#2327; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; 15% &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 450 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2376;&#2358;&#2348;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2349;&#2368; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 10% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 1800 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2376;&#2327; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; (2 &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 2482.42", "Rs. 2376.12", "Rs. 2858.82", "Rs. 2732.32"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 2482.42", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2376.12", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2858.82", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2732.32"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>S.P = C.P * 110/100 = 1800 * 110/100 = Rs. 1980 </p><p>Discount Price = Tag Price * (100  -  15)/100 = 85 * Tag Price/100 </p><p>S.P = Discount Price  -  Cashback </p><p>1980 = 85 * Tag Price/100  -  450 </p><p>Tag Price = Rs. 2858.82 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>S.P = C.P * 110/100 = 1800 * 110/100 = Rs. 1980 </p><p>Discount Price = Tag Price * (100  -  15)/100 = 85 * Tag Price/100 </p><p>S.P = Discount Price  -  Cashback </p><p>1980 = 85 * Tag Price/100  -  450 </p><p>Tag Price = Rs. 2858.82 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper wanted to sell Rs. 3000 worth of products. But he had two options, giving three successive discounts of 15% each or giving a single discount of 34%. What was the difference between the two options of discounts (in rupees)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; 3000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2341;&#2375;, 15% &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366; &#2351;&#2366; 34% &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366;&#2404; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; (&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 132.225", "Rs. 141.625", "Rs. 146.225", "Rs. 137.625"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 132.225", "&#2352;&#2369;. 141.625", "&#2352;&#2369;. 146.225", "&#2352;&#2369;. 137.625"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Equivalent discount = 1  -  (1  -  0.15) * (1  -  0.15) * (1  -  0.15) </p><p>= 0.385875 = 38.5875% </p><p>Difference in discount = 38.5875  -  34 = 4.5875% </p><p>Hence, the required difference = 3000 * 4.5875/100 = Rs. 137.625</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Equivalent discount = 1  -  (1  -  0.15) * (1  -  0.15) * (1  -  0.15) </p><p>= 0.385875 = 38.5875% </p><p>Difference in discount = 38.5875  -  34 = 4.5875% </p><p>Hence, the required difference = 3000 * 4.5875/100 = Rs. 137.625</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The cost price of 31 articles is the same as the selling price of X articles. If the profit is 24%, then the value of X is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>31 &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; X &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 24% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["30", "35", "25", "20"], "options_hi": ["30", "35", "25", "20"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the C.P. of 1 article be Rs. 'a'.</p><p>C.P of 31 articles = Rs. 31a </p><p>S.P of X articles = Rs. 31a </p><p>S.P of 1 article = C.P * (100 + Profit)/100 = a * 124/100 = Rs. 1.24a</p><p>S.P of X article = X * 1.24a </p><p>31a = 1.24a * X</p><p>X = 25 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the C.P. of 1 article be Rs. 'a'.</p><p>C.P of 31 articles = Rs. 31a </p><p>S.P of X articles = Rs. 31a </p><p>S.P of 1 article = C.P * (100 + Profit)/100 = a * 124/100 = Rs. 1.24a</p><p>S.P of X article = X * 1.24a </p><p>31a = 1.24a * X</p><p>X = 25 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Kajal owns an article worth Rs. 18000. He sells it to Ekta at a profit of 18%. After some days, Ekta sells it back to Kajal at a 20% loss. Find the percentage profit or loss faced by Kajal.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2366;&#2332;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; 18000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; 18% &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2319;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2332;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2366;&#2332;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["21.5%", "24.2%", "22.9%", "23.6%"], "options_hi": ["21.5%", "24.2%", "22.9%", "23.6%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>C.P (Kajal) = Rs. 18000</p><p>S.P (Kajal) = 18000 * 118/100 = Rs. 21240 </p><p>S.P (Ekta) = 21240 * 80/100 = Rs. 16992 </p><p>Total profit of Kajal = 21240  -  18000 + (18000  -  16992) = Rs. 4248</p><p>Hence, the profit percent = 4248 * 100/18000 = 23.6%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>C.P (Kajal) = Rs. 18000</p><p>S.P (Kajal) = 18000 * 118/100 = Rs. 21240 </p><p>S.P (Ekta) = 21240 * 80/100 = Rs. 16992 </p><p>Total profit of Kajal = 21240  -  18000 + (18000  -  16992) = Rs. 4248</p><p>Hence, the profit percent = 4248 * 100/18000 = 23.6%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A merchant bought two articles for Rs. 8500 each. He sold one article at a loss of 12%. At what price (in Rs.) should he sell the other article to earn a profit of 16% overall?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; 8500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; 12% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 16% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; (&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 12240", "Rs. 12440", "Rs. 12340", "Rs. 12540"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 12240", "&#2352;&#2369;. 12440", "&#2352;&#2369;. 12340", "&#2352;&#2369;. 12540"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>S.P of 1<sup>st</sup> article = 8500 * 88/100 = Rs. 7480 </p><p>S.P of both articles = (8500 * 2) * 116/100 = Rs. 19720 </p><p>S.P of 2<sup>nd</sup> article = 19720  -  7480 = Rs. 12240 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>S.P of 1<sup>st</sup> article = 8500 * 88/100 = Rs. 7480 </p><p>S.P of both articles = (8500 * 2) * 116/100 = Rs. 19720 </p><p>S.P of 2<sup>nd</sup> article = 19720  -  7480 = Rs. 12240 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper purchased 20 kg rice for Rs. 1600. He spends some amount on transportation and then sells it for Rs. 2400. If the percentage of profit made by the shopkeeper is 28%, then what is the amount (in Rs.) he spends on transportation?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 1600 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 20 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2361;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 2400 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 28% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2361;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; (&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 325", "Rs. 275", "Rs. 225", "Rs. 375"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 325", "&#2352;&#2369;. 275", "&#2352;&#2369;. 225", "&#2352;&#2369;. 375"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>C.P = S.P * 100/(100 + Profit)</p><p>= 2400 * 100/128 </p><p>= Rs. 1875 </p><p>Spends amount on transportation = 1875  -  1600 = Rs. 275 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>C.P = S.P * 100/(100 + Profit)</p><p>= 2400 * 100/128 </p><p>= Rs. 1875 </p><p>Spends amount on transportation = 1875  -  1600 = Rs. 275 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper buys apples at the rate of 16 apples for Rs. 80 and sells them at the rate of 21 apples for Rs. 117. Find his gain or loss percentage.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; 80 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2348; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; 117 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 21 &#2360;&#2375;&#2348; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["11 (3/7)% loss", "13 (5/6)% profit", "11(3/7)% profit", "13 (5/6)% loss"], "options_hi": ["11 (3/7)% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;", "13 (5/6)% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "11(3/7)% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "13 (5/6)% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>C.P of 21 apples = 80 * 21/16 = Rs. 105 </p><p>S.P of 21 apples = Rs. 117 </p><p>Profit% = (117  -  105) * 100/105 = 11(3/7) %</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>C.P of 21 apples = 80 * 21/16 = Rs. 105 </p><p>S.P of 21 apples = Rs. 117 </p><p>Profit% = (117  -  105) * 100/105 = 11(3/7) %</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The cost price of the two articles is equal. One article is sold at a profit of 18% and the other article for Rs. 2100 more than the first. If the net profit is 20(1/2) %, then what is the cost price of each article?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; 18% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; 2100 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 20(1/2)% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 42000", "Rs. 36000", "Rs. 45000", "Rs. 39000"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 42000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 36000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 45000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 39000"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the C.P. of each article be Rs. 'X'</p><p>S.P of 1<sup>st</sup> article = X * 118/100 = Rs. 1.18X</p><p>S.P of 2<sup>nd</sup> article = Rs. 1.18X + 2100 </p><p>2X * (100 + 41/2)/100 = 2.36X + 2100 </p><p>X * 241/100 = 2.36X + 2100 </p><p>0.05X = 2100 </p><p>X = Rs. 42000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the C.P. of each article be Rs. 'X'</p><p>S.P of 1<sup>st</sup> article = X * 118/100 = Rs. 1.18X</p><p>S.P of 2<sup>nd</sup> article = Rs. 1.18X + 2100 </p><p>2X * (100 + 41/2)/100 = 2.36X + 2100 </p><p>X * 241/100 = 2.36X + 2100 </p><p>0.05X = 2100 </p><p>X = Rs. 42000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>By selling 45 m of cloth a shopkeeper makes a profit equivalent to the selling price of 15 m of cloth. Find the selling price of 1 m of cloth when the cost price of 1 m of cloth is Rs. 840.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>45 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; 15 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 1 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; 1 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 840 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 1440", "Rs. 1260", "Rs. 1320", "Rs. 1180"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 1440", "&#2352;&#2369;. 1260", "&#2352;&#2369;. 1320", "&#2352;&#2369;. 1180"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the S.P. of 1 m clothes be Rs. X.</p><p>S.P of 45 m clothes = Rs. 45X</p><p>Profit on selling 45 m clothes = 45X  -  45 * 840</p><p>15X = 45X  -  45 * 840 </p><p>30X = 45 * 840 </p><p>X = Rs. 1260 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the S.P. of 1 m clothes be Rs. X.</p><p>S.P of 45 m clothes = Rs. 45X</p><p>Profit on selling 45 m clothes = 45X  -  45 * 840</p><p>15X = 45X  -  45 * 840 </p><p>30X = 45 * 840 </p><p>X = Rs. 1260 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A seller decreased the selling price of each item from 6000 to 5640, by which his loss percentage increased by 8%. If he has to get 8% profit, then the selling price of the item should be:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 6000 &#2360;&#2375; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 5640 &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 8% &#2348;&#2338;&#2364; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 8% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;:</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 4500", "Rs. 4680", "Rs. 4860", "Rs. 4200"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 4500", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4680", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4860", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4200"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let C.P. be Rs. X</p><p>Loss% = (C.P  -  S.P) * 100/C. P</p><p>Initial loss % = (X  -  6000) * 100/X</p><p>Final loss % = (X  -  5640) * 100/X </p><p>Initial loss + 8 = Final loss</p><p>(X  -  6000) * 100/X + 8 = (X  -  5640) * 100/X</p><p>100X  -  564000  -  100X + 600000 = 8X </p><p>8X = 36000</p><p>X = 4500 </p><p>Hence, the required S.P = 4500 * 108/100 = Rs. 4860 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let C.P. be Rs. X</p><p>Loss% = (C.P  -  S.P) * 100/C. P</p><p>Initial loss % = (X  -  6000) * 100/X</p><p>Final loss % = (X  -  5640) * 100/X </p><p>Initial loss + 8 = Final loss</p><p>(X  -  6000) * 100/X + 8 = (X  -  5640) * 100/X</p><p>100X  -  564000  -  100X + 600000 = 8X </p><p>8X = 36000</p><p>X = 4500 </p><p>Hence, the required S.P = 4500 * 108/100 = Rs. 4860 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A retailer purchased a batch of goods for Rs. 7500. Due to a manufacturing defect, 10% of the goods were damaged. If the retailer wants to make a profit of 30% on the remaining goods, at what price should the undamaged goods be sold?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; 7500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2376;&#2330; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;&#2339; &#2342;&#2379;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339;, 10% &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2340;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2326;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2346;&#2352; 30% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2340;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 9750", "Rs. 8025", "Rs. 9000", "Rs. 8775"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 9750", "&#2352;&#2369;. 8025", "&#2352;&#2369;. 9000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 8775"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>C.P of undamaged goods = 7500 * 90/100 = Rs. 6750</p><p>Hence, the required S.P = 6750 * 130/100 </p><p>= Rs. 8775</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>C.P of undamaged goods = 7500 * 90/100 = Rs. 6750</p><p>Hence, the required S.P = 6750 * 130/100 </p><p>= Rs. 8775</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A person bought X dozens of banana at total Rs. 3024 and sold each banana at Rs. 12. If the amount of profit received by him is Rs. 1008. Find the value of X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 3024 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; X &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; 12 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 1008 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["26", "28", "30", "32"], "options_hi": ["26", "28", "30", "32"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total cost price = 3024</p><p>Total selling price = 3024 + 1008 = Rs. 4032</p><p>Selling price of each banana = 4032/12X = 12</p><p>X = 4032/(12 * 12) = 28</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total cost price = 3024</p><p>Total selling price = 3024 + 1008 = Rs. 4032</p><p>Selling price of each banana = 4032/12X = 12</p><p>X = 4032/(12 * 12) = 28</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Madhu bought an article for Rs. X. The percentage of profit and loss after selling the article for Rs. 2645 and Rs. 1955 respectively is same. The value of X is :</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2343;&#2369; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2352;&#2369;. X &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2404; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2352;&#2369;. 2645 &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;. 1955 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376; :</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 2450", "Rs. 2400", "Rs. 2250", "Rs. 2300"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 2450", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2400", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2250", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2300"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let </p><p>According to question,</p><p>(2645  -  X)/X * 100 = (X  -  1955)/X * 100</p><p>2645  -  X = X  -  1955</p><p>2X = 4600</p><p>X = Rs. 2300</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let </p><p>According to question,</p><p>(2645  -  X)/X * 100 = (X  -  1955)/X * 100</p><p>2645  -  X = X  -  1955</p><p>2X = 4600</p><p>X = Rs. 2300</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A mango seller makes a profit of 30% by selling Alphonso mangoes at a certain price. If he charges Rs 2 more per Alphonso, he would gain 50%. Find the original price of mango?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2350; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;&#2306;&#2360;&#2379; &#2310;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2325;&#2352; 30% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;&#2306;&#2360;&#2379; &#2310;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352; 2 &#2352;&#2369; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2358;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 50% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;| &#2310;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs 12", "Rs 10", "Rs 11", "Rs 18"], "options_hi": ["12 &#2352;&#2369;", "10 &#2352;&#2369;", "11 &#2352;&#2369;", "18 &#2352;&#2369;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the original price of mango be X.</p><p>Now it is given that if we add Rs 2 to the selling price, the profit will get an increase from 30% to 50%.</p><p>Therefore we can say that 20% = Rs 2.</p><p>So the original price of mango, i.e 100% = (100  *  2)/20 = Rs 10</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the original price of mango be X.</p><p>Now it is given that if we add Rs 2 to the selling price, the profit will get an increase from 30% to 50%.</p><p>Therefore we can say that 20% = Rs 2.</p><p>So the original price of mango, i.e 100% = (100  *  2)/20 = Rs 10</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following is a better deal for a customer?</p><p>A. 10 successive discounts of 4%</p><p>B. 1 whole discount of 40%</p><p>C. 4 successive discounts of 10%</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366;/&#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2348;&#2375;&#2361;&#2340;&#2352; &#2360;&#2380;&#2342;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>A. 4% &#2325;&#2368; 10 &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335;</p><p>B. 40% &#2325;&#2368; 1 &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335;</p><p>C. 10% &#2325;&#2368; 4 &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335;</p>", "options_en": ["A", "B", "C", "Both A and B"], "options_hi": ["A", "B", "C", "A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>A. Price after 1st discount = 0.96SP</p><p>Price after 2nd discount = 0.9216SP</p><p>Total discount = 7.84%</p><p>Thus we see that 2 discounts &lt; 8%</p><p>Similarly 10 discounts &lt; 40%</p><p>B. 40%</p><p>C. Price after 1st discount =0.9SP</p><p>Price after 2<sup>nd</sup> discount =0.81SP</p><p>Total discount = 19%</p><p>2 discount &lt; 20%</p><p>4 discount &lt; 40%</p><p>Thus, we can clearly say that option B will be cheapest to the customer.</p><p>Hence the correct option is B.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A. Price after 1st discount = 0.96SP</p><p>Price after 2nd discount = 0.9216SP</p><p>Total discount = 7.84%</p><p>Thus we see that 2 discounts &lt; 8%</p><p>Similarly 10 discounts &lt; 40%</p><p>B. 40%</p><p>C. Price after 1st discount =0.9SP</p><p>Price after 2<sup>nd</sup> discount =0.81SP</p><p>Total discount = 19%</p><p>2 discount &lt; 20%</p><p>4 discount &lt; 40%</p><p>Thus, we can clearly say that option B will be cheapest to the customer.</p><p>Hence the correct option is B.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}]}